3. **Check your credit score and address any issues well before application.** Contractors don't have employer-sponsored credit benefits. Your credit profile is entirely your own responsibility, and improvement takes time. Start early.  
4. **Build your liquid reserves beyond just the down payment.** Lenders require documented reserves after closing. Building reserves consistently over 12 to 24 months is cleaner than a large deposit shortly before application.  
5. **Calculate both your conventional and Non-QM qualifying income 6 to 12 months before your target purchase date.** Know which product fits your income profile before you're under contract on a property and time-pressured to close.  
6. **Avoid taking on new debt in the 12 months before you apply.** New car loans, personal loans, or significant credit card balances change your debt-to-income picture. Decisions made a year before your application still show up in underwriting.

