A standard foreign national loan requires income documentation from your home country, which means translated tax returns, employer letters or business financials, and a credit report from a foreign bureau. A DSCR loan for a foreign national investor typically requires a valid passport, proof of funds for the down payment and reserves, and documentation that the property generates sufficient rental income to meet the coverage ratio.

