Most mortgage products require a down payment, charge private mortgage insurance if your equity is below a certain threshold, and qualify you based on a debt-to-income ratio that often leaves little room for the realities of military pay and service-related income. The VA loan eliminates all three of those constraints simultaneously. Eligible borrowers can purchase a home with no down payment, pay no private mortgage insurance regardless of how much equity they hold, and qualify under guidelines that are specifically designed to account for military compensation structures. No other widely available mortgage program offers all three of those features together.

