Private mortgage insurance on a conventional loan with a low down payment typically costs between 0.5% and 1.5% of the loan amount annually. On a home in the mid-range of most markets, that’s several thousand dollars per year added to the cost of carrying the mortgage, for years, until enough equity is built to remove it. The VA loan eliminates that cost for the life of the loan regardless of the down payment amount. Over a typical loan term, that elimination represents a significant financial advantage.

